# RRT + Behavior-Cloning campaign — statistics

Source: results_rrtbc.csv (960 episodes). Faithful method: RRT expert routes + trained BC local policy + route reuse. Collisions = blocked-move (3-step-lookahead-into-obstacle) events. Episodes run to steps=2000 (~245 completed tasks at 5 agents), so the shared collision database fills and comparisons have power.


## Skill transfer on Map2 (hybrid; Map2-naive 'original' vs Map2-adapted 'alternative')
- 2 agents: original coll 279.07 ± 36.92 (per-task 3.02, fail-rate 0.20); alternative coll 41.20 ± 17.97 (per-task 0.42, fail-rate 0.06); adaptation cuts collisions 85% (MWU original>alt p=1.5e-11, perm p=0.0001).
- 4 agents: original coll 718.50 ± 61.57 (per-task 4.08, fail-rate 0.23); alternative coll 210.03 ± 33.93 (per-task 1.11, fail-rate 0.08); adaptation cuts collisions 71% (MWU original>alt p=1.5e-11, perm p=0.0001).
- 6 agents: original coll 1272.13 ± 94.33 (per-task 5.01, fail-rate 0.26); alternative coll 573.37 ± 68.98 (per-task 2.09, fail-rate 0.12); adaptation cuts collisions 55% (MWU original>alt p=1.51e-11, perm p=0.0001).
- 8 agents: original coll 1942.27 ± 124.38 (per-task 5.92, fail-rate 0.29); alternative coll 1045.27 ± 87.37 (per-task 3.00, fail-rate 0.16); adaptation cuts collisions 46% (MWU original>alt p=1.51e-11, perm p=0.0001).
- 10 agents: original coll 2688.93 ± 113.24 (per-task 6.75, fail-rate 0.32); alternative coll 1653.73 ± 104.81 (per-task 3.87, fail-rate 0.18); adaptation cuts collisions 38% (MWU original>alt p=1.51e-11, perm p=0.0001).

## Collision-history sharing — ablation on map1 (5 agents)
- none: collisions 366.83 ± 64.43 | per-task 1.45 | tasks 253.70 ± 10.06
- selective 0.6: collisions 332.80 ± 53.07 | per-task 1.34 | tasks 249.30 ± 9.98
- full 1.0: collisions 338.57 ± 58.14 | per-task 1.38 | tasks 244.97 ± 8.88
- selective reduces collisions 9% vs none (MWU none>selective p=0.0242).
- full reduces collisions 8% vs none (MWU none>full p=0.0466).
- full>selective one-sided p=0.401 (selective better (migration under full)).

## Collision-history sharing — ablation on map2 (5 agents)
- none: collisions 379.90 ± 62.38 | per-task 1.64 | tasks 233.20 ± 8.10
- selective 0.6: collisions 373.80 ± 48.55 | per-task 1.62 | tasks 231.43 ± 10.58
- full 1.0: collisions 361.87 ± 61.65 | per-task 1.56 | tasks 233.27 ± 8.60
- selective reduces collisions 2% vs none (MWU none>selective p=0.432).
- full reduces collisions 5% vs none (MWU none>full p=0.156).
- full>selective one-sided p=0.861 (no migration).

## Access-fraction sweep (Map1, 5 agents)
- p=0.0: collisions 366.83 ± 64.43 | per-task 1.45
- p=0.2: collisions 351.10 ± 72.24 | per-task 1.38
- p=0.4: collisions 358.77 ± 52.67 | per-task 1.43
- p=0.6: collisions 332.80 ± 53.07 | per-task 1.34
- p=0.8: collisions 338.03 ± 39.65 | per-task 1.37
- p=1.0: collisions 338.57 ± 58.14 | per-task 1.38
- Spearman ρ(p, collisions-per-task) = -0.06 (p=0.439); minimum at p=0.6.

## Sharing scalability (Map1, none vs selective 0.6)
- no sharing: ρ(fleet, tasks)=0.98 (p=1.7e-105); coll-per-task 0.11..4.11
- selective ($q_{\mathrm{share}}=0.6$): ρ(fleet, tasks)=0.98 (p=1.6e-105); coll-per-task 0.16..3.98

## Sharing multiple-comparison correction (Holm across the 4 ablation tests)
- map1 share=0.6: nominal p=0.0242, perm p=0.0143, Holm p=0.0968, n.s. after correction.
- map1 share=1.0: nominal p=0.0466, perm p=0.0412, Holm p=0.14, n.s. after correction.
- map2 share=0.6: nominal p=0.432, perm p=0.343, Holm p=0.432, n.s. after correction.
- map2 share=1.0: nominal p=0.156, perm p=0.13, Holm p=0.311, n.s. after correction.

## Post-hoc power analysis (bootstrap-simulated Mann-Whitney, 2000 iterations)
- map1 selective=0.6: post-hoc power at n=30 per arm = 0.62
- map1 full=1.0: post-hoc power at n=30 per arm = 0.53
- map2 selective=0.6: post-hoc power at n=30 per arm = 0.07
- map2 full=1.0: post-hoc power at n=30 per arm = 0.26
- map1 full: minimal detectable collision reduction with >=0.80 power at n=30 per arm = 15% of the no-sharing mean.

